    "chunk_size_bytes": 2326,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9a\u0dc1\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dcf, \u0dc1\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dd3\u0dba\u0dc0 \u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dd3\u0dba\u0dc00 \u0d92 \u0dc1\u0dad\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba\u0dda\u0da7 \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dc0 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db0\u0dd2\u0dba\u0da7 \u0dba) \u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dd4 \u0dc1 \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dc2\u0dab - \u0db8\u0dd8\u0dd4 \u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dad \u0dc1 \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dc2\u0dab - \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dad \u0dc3\u0dc0 consumer jurisdiction \u0d91 \u0dad\u0db8\u0dba\u0dd2 tax \u0d91 \u0da7 \u0d85\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0db8 \u0dc1\u0dc0\u0da7 \u0dc1\u0da7 0 \u0d91\u0dc1\u0dc4\u0db8 \u0dad\u0db8\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0dad\u0dca \u0dc2\u0dab \u0dc3\u0da7\u0dc0\u0dbd\u0dba\u0dda \u0dc3\u0da7 \u0dc1\u0da7 0\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Chairman) \u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4 \u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dcf0\n\nSir, I would like to say a few more words about that sector and finish my speech. There have been questions on VAT being applied at 18 per cent on this whole sector. I would like to say that IT services provided to persons outside Sri Lanka, for which payments are received in foreign currency, are exempt from Income Tax. The supply of IT services was liable to VAT until 31st December, 2019 and was exempt from VAT only from 01st of January, 2020. IT services will be liable for VAT, effective from 01st January, 2024 by the new Amendment. However, making IT services liable for VAT will not become a burden to the industry since those IT companies are export-oriented and export of IT services is a zero-rated supply. Furthermore, even in India, the GST rate for all kinds of IT software supply services and products are 18 per cent. We have decided, as a policy, to increase the VAT up to 18 per cent. Then, it must apply to all sectors; you cannot exempt some sectors and apply it to others.\n\nNow, many in the IT sector have said that they can go ahead, provided certain assistance is given to them. Some of the others are complaining, but they have always been complaining. When we tried, in 2003, to bring the Tata Group in to digitalize the revenue collections and the home affairs services, they all complained. But now, they say they can do it. To date, we have had nothing. Now, we are still piggybacking on Aadhaar system after 20 years. Similarly, when we started this in 2015, there was a big debate as to whether you need foreign personnel and that was the biggest debate, not how we should increase it. Finally, there were no foreign personnel. Half the people who shouted then are now leaving the country. So,"
