    "chunk_text": "Now, many in the IT sector have said that they can go ahead, provided certain assistance is given to them. Some of the others are complaining, but they have always been complaining. When we tried, in 2003, to bring the Tata Group in to digitalize the revenue collections and the home affairs services, they all complained. But now, they say they can do it. To date, we have had nothing. Now, we are still piggybacking on Aadhaar system after 20 years. Similarly, when we started this in 2015, there was a big debate as to whether you need foreign personnel and that was the biggest debate, not how we should increase it. Finally, there were no foreign personnel. Half the people who shouted then are now leaving the country. So,\n\nWe should expand on artificial intelligence. Otherwise, we will be competing with Myanmar to have low-income, low-wage manufacturing.\n\nSo, the new agency will be the Digital Transformation Agency, and they will do the policy work. Like ICTA, they will not get involved in project management. That was built - I think the Hon. Eran Wickramaratne knows that - and was to be there for 10 years, and then they kept extending it. But, now, you need a new agency and within that there will be the AI centre. The other one is the Digital Technology and Innovation Council, which will look at commercializing innovations in the field of technology. They are the people who will use that Rs. 8 billion, of which a part would go for research in IT and the rest for the other sectors. So, they will certainly work on this field."
