    "chunk_text": "So, the new agency will be the Digital Transformation Agency, and they will do the policy work. Like ICTA, they will not get involved in project management. That was built - I think the Hon. Eran Wickramaratne knows that - and was to be there for 10 years, and then they kept extending it. But, now, you need a new agency and within that there will be the AI centre. The other one is the Digital Technology and Innovation Council, which will look at commercializing innovations in the field of technology. They are the people who will use that Rs. 8 billion, of which a part would go for research in IT and the rest for the other sectors. So, they will certainly work on this field.\n\nConnected to that is agricultural modernization. Modernization of agriculture is, again, increasing productivity and applying of technology. We are going to apply technology to agriculture and part of this money would be available for the application of technology in agriculture. We have a limited land space available. So,\n\n3771 3772\n\n[\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca \u0daf\u0dca\u200d \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0daf\u0dca\u200d \u0dd0)\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\nwe have to use it to the maximum. To maximize our output, we must also use technology. That is the second area and we are bringing in the University of Colombo\u2019s Institute for Agro-technology and Rural Sciences, which will update the research institutions and work to back up the modernization scheme in Sri Lanka. We are combining the private sector and the public sector together. In most areas, whether it be tea, paddy or other crops, our productivity is low. So, we have to increase productivity. Then, there are problems, as you know, with regard to rubber. There are many issues that we have to resolve in the rubber sector."
  },
