    "md5": "d9fb94f67e0cf9825407537e8b647ee8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1828,
    "chunk_text": "We did not build pyramids; we built semi-circular dagobas, which were far more difficult to build. We had built forts like Sigiriya, which has an amazing hydraulic system. So, look at the combination we had in engineering, that no other country could show any constructions with all that. The only other country which had those skills had been China; China and us. We are a small country, but we have the potential.\n\nThen, with regard to investments, we would bring in laws which would make the necessary changes sometime in January or February. The BOI and the EDB would be scrapped and would be replaced by the Economic Commission, which would draw investments in to all the fields in the country. It would be done quite differently from what we are doing now. I will brief the Members of the House at that time. The industrial estates and investment zones would be separated. Then, there would be an Investment Infrastructure Corporation which would set up the investment promotion zones. We would allow the private sector or the Government to do it and all of them would be registered as public companies. Then, they would provide the services. The Corporation will oversee and regulate those investment zones. There would also be an International Trade Centre, which would deal with international trade. Those three institutions would be connected to each other and that is basically going to be the new structure for foreign investments.\n\nThen, we are looking at amending the Colombo Port City Economic Commission Act to make the Port City\n\n3773 3774\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1)\u0da7 \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\ninto a Financial City. We have got the draft from Shearman & Sterling LLP; they have updated it and are doing the regulations. All of you will be able to go through the new draft, which will make provisions for offshore financing."
  },
