    "chunk_text": "into a Financial City. We have got the draft from Shearman & Sterling LLP; they have updated it and are doing the regulations. All of you will be able to go through the new draft, which will make provisions for offshore financing.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0daf\u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0dd9\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9c\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb0\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb8) (The Hon. Sajith Premadasa) Thank you very much, Hon. President, for your presentation with regard to investment and technology. I just have one or two queries, if I may explore you.\n\nYour attempt to increase the number of universities in the technology field and elsewhere is a good proposal and a good attempt to enhance technological education in Sri Lanka. However, I want to bring to your notice that right now, in the State university system, where we are supposed to have 12,000 teaching personnel, whether it be professors, lecturers and so on and so forth, the cadre provision is 8,000, but presently, the numbers hover around 5,000 because a large number of them have gone for international internship programmes and also on sabbaticals. Hon. President, I can understand your intention, improving the number of students, but however, we need to find the relevant teaching personnel as well."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
