    "date_str": "2023-12-12",
    "description": "Hansard of December 12, 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1709099289047167.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-12-12-2023-12-12-0085",
    "chunk_index": 85,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "87ad009cbac1d1ae40b7e157a3510bb6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2137,
    "chunk_text": "Your attempt to increase the number of universities in the technology field and elsewhere is a good proposal and a good attempt to enhance technological education in Sri Lanka. However, I want to bring to your notice that right now, in the State university system, where we are supposed to have 12,000 teaching personnel, whether it be professors, lecturers and so on and so forth, the cadre provision is 8,000, but presently, the numbers hover around 5,000 because a large number of them have gone for international internship programmes and also on sabbaticals. Hon. President, I can understand your intention, improving the number of students, but however, we need to find the relevant teaching personnel as well.\n\nThe second issue, Hon. President, is that when you increase the number of students without increasing the number of teachers, the student: teacher ratio becomes a\n\nmuddle, the ratio becomes very big. When that happens, the international ratings of our universities are downgraded. I can give you two examples. The University of Peradeniya and the University of Colombo, which hovered earlier among the top 500 in those rankings, have now been downgraded beyond the thousand level, I believe to the level of the 1,200 universities. That is because the brain drain has impacted on this situation with the teachers going abroad.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Chairman) \u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0d9a\u0dba\u0dd2, \u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dc2\u0dab \u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dba \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db8\u0dcf0 \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0daf\u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0dd9\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9c\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb0\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb8) (The Hon. Sajith Premadasa) And, the last thing I want to point out is this. Hon. President, you may increase the number of students, but they do not have the facilities in universities. You need to give them human resources, physical facilities and equipment in order to make sure those universities are of high standards. So, I just wanted to raise those issues since you are here. Thank you for your presentation, Hon. President."
  },
