    "chunk_size_bytes": 2083,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Presiding Member, it was really Charles Babbage who, in 1860, invented the analytical engine that was actually known as the first computer. So, with that, technological advancement really started in terms of computers and digital technology. Today, Sir, the buzzword is \"artificial intelligence\" - \u0dd8\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0db8 \u0db6\u0dd4\u0dd2\u0db0\u0dd2\u0dba0 Leading nations such as the United States and China led their economic growth based on modern technology. The two Ministries that are being debated today are most important, the Cabinet Minister of which is none other than the Hon. President.\n\nTherefore, with this technology, a tool for anti-corruption could be adopted by your Ministry. We are talking in Parliament about various acts of corruption, corrupt deals that had taken place and tenders that had not been correctly awarded. All these could be rectified, if we look at adopting technology as a mode for anti-corruption. Hon. State Minister, my father had worked very closely with your father. I am happy that you are handling a Ministry of this nature. I wish you success but, at the same time, a lot of work has to be done and I think being a young State Minister, you are capable of doing that. I think you have got a staff that supports you. So, again, let me wish you every success.\n\nWhen talking of technology and Estonia, today, another country which is using technology even for its war is Ukraine. Ukraine has an App of this nature that they have developed and they are able to fight the war today using that App. That App is used not just for what it was created, but in terms of giving information to people about the war situation. So, they are able to fight with a superpower like Russia, not just because they have the military capabilities, but also technological advancement.\n\nIf you look at India, for example, they had allocated 1.5 per cent of their GDP on technology in the 2023 Budget. Then, countries like Singapore, Korea and even\n\n3847 3848\n\n[\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dba\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dab\u0dd3 \u0dc0\u0dda\u0db4\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db1\u0dc0 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0daf\u0dca\u200d \u0dd0)\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca 12"
  },
