    "chunk_size_bytes": 2099,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dd2\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0da2\u0dba\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0da2\u0db4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf (\u0b95\u0bc8\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0bc7\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb8 \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0bc7\u0baa\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bb7) (The Hon. (Dr.) Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe, PC) It was not this Bill. That was the TRC Bill. This is a different one.\n\nAnyway, what I was trying to point out was that there was a discussion held. When that Bill was also brought forward, we raised that there was no judicial mechanism in that. So, with no judicial mechanism in that Bill, we, as the Representatives of the victim community, rejected that and from then onwards, we still have not heard back from anybody as to how the justice mechanism is going to be included into that Bill. When we had the most recent meeting with the Hon. President also, we brought his attention to the fact that no changes had been made to it and the Hon. President said, \u201cWe will discuss about that\u201d. But still, there is no progress on that as well.\n\nSo, again and again, what we see, Hon. Minister, is that there are various Bills being brought in to set up various offices. This Bill, I see again as one of those Bills that has been brought forward as mere eyewash. There are no real reconciliation efforts on the ground, there is no reconciliation happening from the Government side, but Bill after Bill is being presented. If we are to be very serious about reconciliation, we need to address the justice mechanism within transitional justice. Without there being any justice-centred approach, any\n\nreconciliation efforts you bring forward would be rejected. You saw that the President went to Jaffna a few days ago and there were massive protests against the President. The President, on the other hand, was chairing the District Development Committee meeting and various other meetings, talking about various matters. But, that was not the primary concern of the people of the Northern Province. When he came to the Eastern Province also, there was a similar response."
  },
