    "md5": "ef8dd9e0c51b5932bd94234cc09b8d59",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1607,
    "chunk_text": "reconciliation efforts you bring forward would be rejected. You saw that the President went to Jaffna a few days ago and there were massive protests against the President. The President, on the other hand, was chairing the District Development Committee meeting and various other meetings, talking about various matters. But, that was not the primary concern of the people of the Northern Province. When he came to the Eastern Province also, there was a similar response.\n\nSir, I have a feeling that the Government has a sadist\u2019s view. Setting up commissions, bringing in reconciliation efforts and relating their stories are to put the victims again under more stress. For them to believe that there is some genuine reconciliation going to happen, the things on the ground must change. You all had arrested people under the Prevention of Terrorism Act on the 28th of November, last year. Four of them had been released and the other six are still in jail. What is reconciliation when the right to memorialize the dead is also being taken away from our people? So, Hon. Minister, in whatever reconciliation efforts you may take, in whatever Bills you may present, if you all are not genuine and sincere and there is no justice mechanism, nothing will come out of it. And, even within the justice mechanism, there has to be some sort of international involvement, there have to be international judges or observers. I think when you were the Minister of Justice between 2015 and 2017 in the previous Government, there was some agreement about international involvement, but all that has been put aside now."
  },
