    "chunk_text": "Therefore, the effect of limiting the import of fertilizer in the year 2021 will be reflected in the coconut yield from the year 2023. As per the forecast of the Coconut Research Institute, the coconut yield in the year 2023 is 2,957 million nuts. That is a decrease of about 434 million nuts compared to the year 2022.\n\n(ii) The steps taken by the Coconut Research\n\nInstitute to increase the coconut production in Sri Lanka are given below:\n\n1. Making the coconut growers aware\n\nthrough the Coconut Cultivation Board to adopt Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) to improve the productivity of coconut cultivation. 2. Taking necessary steps to increase\n\nthe number of seedlings produced from the high-quality hybrid coconut varieties produced per year As well, the steps taken by the Coconut Cultivation Board to increase the coconut production in Sri Lanka from 2016 to 2023 (November) are given below:\n\n(1) During the period from 2016 to 2023 (November), the Coconut Cultivation Board has provided 21.33 million coconut seedlings to the coconut growers at a concessionary price. The number of coconut seedlings provided annually is given in the table below.\n\nYear Coconut Seedlings (Millions)\n\n2016 2.62\n\n2017 3.84\n\n2018 2.46\n\n2019 1.92\n\n2020 1.98\n\n2021 2.50\n\n2022 3.51\n\n2023 2.5 (November)\n\n221 222\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dd9\n\n(2) Subsidies have been provided annually to coconut growers to encourage the growers to carry out the following field activities to increase the coconut production.\n\n\uf0d8 Fertilizer subsidy \uf0d8 Providing subsidies for moisture conservation in coconut lands.\n\n\uf0b7 Mulching \uf0b7 Preparing coconut husk pits. \uf0b7 Constructing contour drains. \uf0b7 Constructing water holes. \uf0b7 Installing irrigation systems. \uf0b7 Providing instructions for disease and\n\npest control and paying compensations for the diseased trees removed.\n\n(3) In addition, the growers have also been informed to carry out the following activities through the extension service:\n\n\uf0b7 Making aware of planting and"
